.TH KSTAR-FMT 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-fmt \- rewrite files in the standard style
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar fmt\fR [\-\-check] <files>...
\fBkstar fmt\fR \-
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Rewrites each file in the standard style. A folder means every .kstar file
inside it, and \fB\-\fR reads a program from standard input and writes the
formatted program to standard output, for editors and scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
change nothing; list the files that need formatting and exit with code 1 if there are any
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar fmt lab1.kstar\fR
format one file in place
.TP
\fBkstar fmt \-\-check .\fR
list the files in this folder that are not formatted
.TP
\fBkstar fmt \- < lab1.kstar\fR
print lab1.kstar formatted, changing nothing
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
